url":"/welcome#the-pieces","content":"`skills.lock`"},"358":{"id":"/welcome-11","page_id":"/welcome","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/welcome#the-pieces","content":"Selected versions, revisions, integrity evidence, and ownership"},"359":{"id":"/welcome-12","page_id":"/welcome","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/welcome#the-pieces","content":"Installed directory"},"360":{"id":"/welcome-13","page_id":"/welcome","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/welcome#the-pieces","content":"Files the agent can discover and read"},"361":{"id":"/welcome-14","page_id":"/welcome","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/welcome#the-pieces","content":"Bundle"},"362":{"id":"/welcome-15","page_id":"/welcome","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/welcome#the-pieces","content":"A versioned ZIP containing a team skill set and its dependency closure"},"363":{"id":"/welcome-16","page_id":"/welcome","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/welcome#choose-the-operation","content":"`skill add` declares and installs a skill from a source."},"364":{"id":"/welcome-17","page_id":"/welcome","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/welcome#choose-the-operation","content":"`project install` restores compatible locked selections and resolves missing coverage."},"365":{"id":"/welcome-18","page_id":"/welcome","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/welcome#choose-the-operation","content":"`project install --lock` restores the locked selection without updating the lock."},"366":{"id":"/welcome-19","page_id":"/welcome","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/welcome#choose-the-operation","content":"`skill update` deliberately resolves changes allowed by the recorded constraints."},"367":{"id":"/welcome-20","page_id":"/welcome","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/welcome#choose-the-operation","content":"`skill remove` removes a direct owner; shared requirements can keep a skill installed."},"368":{"id":"/welcome-21","page_id":"/welcome","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/welcome#choose-the-operation","content":"`skill list --check` verifies the desired, locked, and installed state."},"369":{"id":"/welcome-22","page_id":"/welcome","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/welcome#choose-the-operation","content":"Start with your first skill. Continue with\nmanifests and scope,\nteam bundles, or agent access."},"370":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","type":"page","content":"Bundle commands","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Share with teams"],"tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command"},"371":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-0","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","content":"Build, install, update, restore, and customize self-contained team skill bundles."},"372":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-1","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#bundle-commands","content":"`bundle` commands"},"373":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-2","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#build-a-bundle","content":"Build a bundle"},"374":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-3","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#install-and-inspect","content":"Install and inspect"},"375":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-4","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#update-a-bundle","content":"Update a bundle"},"376":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-5","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#remove-a-bundle","content":"Remove a bundle"},"377":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-6","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#personal-overrides","content":"Personal overrides"},"378":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-7","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#bundle-commands","content":"Bundles turn a selected team setup into one versioned ZIP. The artifact contains the selected\nskills, their installed dependency closure, resource files, and content digests. A recipient can\ninstall it without access to the original repositories."},"379":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-8","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#build-a-bundle","content":"Complete the quickstart, then add this declaration to that project's\nexisting `skill-project.toml`. Keep its `[dependencies]` and `[tool.fastskill]` sections."},"380":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-9","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#build-a-bundle","content":"Every bundle member must also appear in `[dependencies]`. The installed member version must\nsatisfy that declaration. FastSkill stops before writing an artifact when a declared member is\nmissing, has invalid frontmatter, or has a different version."},"381":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-10","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#build-a-bundle","content":"Build the release:"},"382":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-11","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#build-a-bundle","content":"The result is `dist/notes-team-1.0.0.zip`. Its embedded identity, version, membership, and\ndigests are authoritative, so renaming the download does not change the release."},"383":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-12","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#install-and-inspect","content":"In a second project initialized with `project init --yes --skills-dir .claude/skills`,\ninstall the artifact with `bundle add`. Replace the local path with the artifact you\nbuilt. The HTTPS URL below is an example for an artifact hosted by your team:"},"384":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-13","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#install-and-inspect","content":"Installation copies the artifact into `.fastskill/bundles/`, adds its declaration to\n`skill-project.toml`, and records the exact release and members in `skills.lock`."},"385":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-14","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#install-and-inspect","content":"Commit these files when teammates and CI need the same setup:"},"386":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-15","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#install-and-inspect","content":"Then restore the exact locked release:"},"387":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-16","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#install-and-inspect","content":"`--lock` uses the bundle artifact, version, digest, and membership recorded in `skills.lock`.\nIt does not switch to a different release if the manifest has drifted. `--offline` additionally\nguarantees that restore does not contact a repository or embedding provider."},"388":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-17","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#update-a-bundle","content":"Bundle updates are explicit. After building version `1.1.0` of your bundle, preview\nand apply that replacement:"},"389":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-18","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#update-a-bundle","content":"FastSkill checks the new artifact, shared ownership, local modifications, and release immutability\nbefore it changes installed members. The preview runs the same validation as apply and reports\npolicy-only changes, such as a member becoming non-overridable, even when its bytes are unchanged."},"390":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-19","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#remove-a-bundle","content":"Remove the bundle identity and the members that have no other owner:"},"391":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-20","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#remove-a-bundle","content":"Removing a direct declaration detaches that owner. FastSkill retains the installed member while a\nbundle or another dependency root still requires it. An ID that is only a transitive requirement\ncannot be removed directly; the error names the roots that require it. A member is deleted only\nafter its final direct, transitive, bundle, and override owner is gone."},"392":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-21","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#personal-overrides","content":"An edited installed file is not an approved override. Put the customized skill in a separate\ndirectory and declare it explicitly. Every installed bundle that owns the skill must mark the\nmember as `overridable = true`."},"393":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-22","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#personal-overrides","content":"`fastskill project install` and `fastskill project install --lock` restore valid personal overrides after\nbundle members. Updates stop when a new bundle policy no longer permits an existing override."},"394":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-23","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#personal-overrides","content":"Return to the packaged member and clear the override records in one operation:"},"395":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-24","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#personal-overrides","content":"Reset is blocked if retained bundles disagree on the packaged bytes or if the installed member has\nuntracked edits. Removing the last bundle owner of a personal replacement keeps that replacement\nas an individual requirement instead of deleting it. FastSkill validates the replacement's complete\ndependency closure first; bundle removal is blocked if that closure cannot be retained."},"396":{"id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command-25","page_id":"/cli-reference/bundle-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/bundle-command#personal-overrides","content":"Every bundle action except `bundle list` changes files. The MCP server hides and refuses these\ntools unless it starts with `fastskill mcp serve --enable-write`."},"397":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","type":"page","content":"cache Command","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Reference","CLI commands","Operations"],"tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/cache-command"},"398":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-0","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command","content":"Inspect and reclaim the on-disk skill content cache with fastskill cache."},"399":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-1","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#cache-command","content":"cache Command"},"400":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-2","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#usage","content":"Usage"},"401":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-3","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#subcommands","content":"Subcommands"},"402":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-4","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#info","content":"info"},"403":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-5","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#clean","content":"clean"},"404":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-6","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#when-to-run-it","content":"When to run it"},"405":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-7","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#see-also","content":"See Also"},"406":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-8","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#cache-command","content":"Inspect and reclaim the on-disk cache that `skill add`, `project install`, and `skill update` use so a skill's\ncontent is fetched once per machine instead of once per project."},"407":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-9","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#cache-command","content":"Every git, registry, or local skill fetch is checked against this cache before touching the\nnetwork again. `fastskill cache` is how to see what has accumulated there and reclaim disk\nspace -- fastskill never evicts cache entries on its own."},"408":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-10","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#info","content":"Show the cache location plus entry counts and disk usage, broken down by source kind (git,\nregistry, or local)."},"409":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-11","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#info","content":"**Example output**:"},"410":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-12","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#info","content":"**Options**:"},"411":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-13","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#info","content":"`--format <table|json>`: Output format (default: table)"},"412":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-14","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#info","content":"`--json`: Shorthand for `--format json` (mutually exclusive with `--format`)"},"413":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-15","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#clean","content":"Remove cached skill content and print how many bytes were reclaimed."},"414":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-16","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#clean","content":"**Options**:"},"415":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-17","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#clean","content":"`--source <git|registry|local>`: Limit cleaning to one source kind (default: all)"},"416":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-18","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#clean","content":"`--json`: Print the result as JSON instead of a summary line"},"417":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-19","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#clean","content":"**What it removes**: Only cached skill content -- the record of what a repository currently\nadvertises (what `repo refresh` writes) is left alone, so `repo refresh` output stays valid\nafter a clean. There is nothing to undo: the next `skill add`/`project install`/`skill update` that needs a removed\nentry re-fetches it from its original source."},"418":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-20","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#clean","content":"**Safe with other fastskill processes running**: `clean` never removes an entry another process\nis mid-write on, and every write elsewhere is atomic. In the worst case, a fetch running at the\nexact moment of a clean simply re-fetches -- it never sees partial or corrupted content."},"419":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-21","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#when-to-run-it","content":"**`cache info`**: Before a `clean`, to see what is actually taking up space, or when disk\nusage seems higher than expected."},"420":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-22","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#when-to-run-it","content":"**`cache clean`**: To reclaim disk space after finishing with skills from a source no longer\nin use, or as routine cleanup on a machine used for many short-lived projects."},"421":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-23","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#see-also","content":"`repo` commands -- refresh what a repository advertises\n(`repo refresh`), independent of the content cache `cache` manages"},"422":{"id":"/cli-reference/cache-command-24","page_id":"/cli-reference/cache-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/cache-command#see-also","content":"Install Command -- installs that hit this cache"},"423":{"id":"/cli-reference/discovery-commands","page_id":"/cli-reference/discovery-commands","type":"page","content":"Discover and inspect skills","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Reference","CLI commands","Sources and distribution"],"tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/discovery-commands"},"424":{"id":"/cli-reference/discovery-commands-0","page_id":"/cli-reference/discovery-commands","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/discovery-commands","content":"Find a catalog result, ins