:{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-10","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#the-metrics-file","content":"The metrics file"},"443":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-11","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#identity-what-the-numbers-are-about","content":"Identity: what the numbers are about"},"444":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-12","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#the-json-document","content":"The JSON document"},"445":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-13","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#the-html-report","content":"The HTML report"},"446":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-14","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#what-is-excluded-and-why","content":"What is excluded, and why"},"447":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-15","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#see-also","content":"See also"},"448":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-16","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#overview","content":"`fastskill eval` runs skill quality checks using prompts and rubrics under `[tool.fastskill.eval]` in `skill-project.toml`. Subcommands are `validate`, `run`, `judge`, `report`, `score`, and `scorecard`."},"449":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-17","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#overview","content":"`eval run` requires an agent on `PATH` for the chosen `--agent` key. Known keys are `aikit`, `claude`, `codex`, `cursor`, `gemini`, and `pi`. A key is accepted only when its CLI is detected on the current machine, so a typo and an uninstalled agent both error with `RUNTIME_UNKNOWN_ID`, which lists what was detected. Use `eval validate --agent <key>` or `--all` to verify availability."},"450":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-18","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-validate","content":"Checks eval configuration and files (optional agent presence check)."},"451":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-19","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-validate","content":"Option"},"452":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-20","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-validate","content":"Description"},"453":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-21","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-validate","content":"`--agent <AGENT>`"},"454":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-22","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-validate","content":"Verify the given agent(s) are available; repeatable. Mutually exclusive with `--all`"},"455":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-23","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-validate","content":"`--all`"},"456":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-24","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-validate","content":"Verify availability of every installed agent. Mutually exclusive with `--agent`"},"457":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-25","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-validate","content":"`--model <MODEL>`"},"458":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-26","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-validate","content":"The model `eval run` will target; a judge declaring the same one is reported as self-preference"},"459":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-27","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-validate","content":"`--format <FORMAT>`"},"460":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-28","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-validate","content":"`table` or `json` only (eval does not support `grid`/`xml`)"},"461":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-29","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-validate","content":"`--json`"},"462":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-30","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-validate","content":"Shorthand for `--format json`"},"463":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-31","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-validate","content":"Every `[[judge]]` in the checks file is validated from file content alone, so validate gives the same answer on a laptop and in CI. Errors: no resolvable `model`; neither or both of `prompt` / `prompt_file` (likewise for the system and retry pairs); an unknown `{{variable}}`; a `cases` id matching no case; duplicate criterion names; `scale` below 2; `min_score` outside `[0, 1]`; a prompt that never renders `{{output_contract}}`; any unknown key. Warnings: a prompt without `{{rubric}}`, and a judge sharing `--model`. Endpoint reachability and API keys are not checked here — judging checks those before its first request."},"464":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-32","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-validate","content":"With `--agent` or `--all`, both outputs report each selected agent:\nthe table prints one `agent '<key>': available|unavailable` line per agent, and the JSON document carries an `agents` object keyed by agent id (`{\"agents\": {\"claude\": true}}`). An unavailable agent is an error unless `fail_on_missing_agent = false` is set in the eval config."},"465":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-33","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-run","content":"Runs eval cases against an agent; writes artifacts under `--output-dir`."},"466":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-34","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-run","content":"`--agent <key>` (repeatable) and `--all` are mutually exclusive — passing both errors with `RUNTIME_CONFLICTING_FLAGS`. `eval run` requires one of them (passing neither errors with `RUNTIME_NO_SELECTION`)."},"467":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-35","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-run","content":"Option"},"468":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-36","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-run","content":"Description"},"469":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-37","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-run","content":"`--agent <AGENT>`"},"470":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-38","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-run","content":"Agent key(s) to run; repeatable. Required unless `--all` is given"},"471":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-39","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-run","content":"`--all`"},"472":{"id":"/cli-reference/eval-command-40","page_id":"/cli-reference/eval-command","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/cli-reference/eval-command#eval-run","content":"Run against all installed agents. Mutually exclusive with `--agent`"},"473":{"