:"/evals-quality/run-evals#re-score-without-re-running-agent","content":"Re-score without re-running agent"},"2055":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-5","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#ci-usage-pattern","content":"CI usage pattern"},"2056":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-6","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#practical-gating-policy","content":"Practical gating policy"},"2057":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-7","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#see-also","content":"See also"},"2058":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-8","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#run-evals","content":"This workflow is the day-to-day path for quality checks. If you haven't authored a suite yet — the `[tool.fastskill.eval]` table, prompts CSV, and checks TOML — start with Eval setup first; pass/fail behavior (especially the inert `should_trigger` column, choosing between `skill_invoked` and `trigger_expectation`, and what `required = false` does) is documented there."},"2059":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-9","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#run-evals","content":"`--output-dir` is required on every `eval run` invocation — there is no default output location. All examples below include it. Each run lands under `<output-dir>/<timestamp>/<agent>/` (a numeric suffix is appended if that timestamp directory already exists) — that per-agent directory, not `<output-dir>` itself, is what `--run-dir` expects below."},"2060":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-10","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#run-the-suite","content":"**Runs are isolated by default.** Each case executes in a per-case scratch workspace containing only the skill under test (`SKILL.md` beside `skill-project.toml`, named by `[metadata].id`), with user-level skill discovery suppressed where the backend supports it. The `isolation:` line in the output (and the `isolation` object in `summary.json`) reports what each run actually got; a failed case's workspace survives under `<run-dir>/workspaces/` for debugging. Pass `--no-isolation` to run in the project root against your machine's ambient environment — and expect trigger rates measured before isolation existed to re-baseline on the first isolated run."},"2061":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-11","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#run-the-suite","content":"Common focused runs:"},"2062":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-12","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#summarize-the-run","content":"Use this for release notes and quick stakeholder review."},"2063":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-13","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#re-score-without-re-running-agent","content":"Use this when scoring logic changed and you want consistency across previous runs."},"2064":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-14","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#practical-gating-policy","content":"Block merge if smoke tag fails"},"2065":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-15","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#practical-gating-policy","content":"Block release if full suite fails"},"2066":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-16","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#practical-gating-policy","content":"Keep per-tag pass-rate trends to detect slow quality drift"},"2067":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-17","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#see-also","content":"Eval setup"},"2068":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-18","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#see-also","content":"Cluster analysis"},"2069":{"id":"/evals-quality/run-evals-19","page_id":"/evals-quality/run-evals","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/run-evals#see-also","content":"eval command"},"2070":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","type":"page","content":"Eval Setup","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Evaluate and optimize","Evaluations"],"tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/setup"},"2071":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-0","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup","content":"Author an eval suite: the [tool.fastskill.eval] manifest table, the prompts CSV, and the checks TOML schema."},"2072":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-1","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/setup#eval-setup","content":"Eval Setup"},"2073":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-2","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/setup#prerequisites","content":"Prerequisites"},"2074":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-3","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"1\\. The `[tool.fastskill.eval]` table"},"2075":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-4","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/setup#validate-the-config","content":"Validate the config"},"2076":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-5","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"2\\. The prompts CSV"},"2077":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-6","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/setup#3-checks-checkstoml-optional","content":"3\\. Checks: `checks.toml` (optional)"},"2078":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-7","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"`skill_invoked`"},"2079":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-8","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"`trigger_expectation`"},"2080":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-9","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"`command_contains`"},"2081":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-10","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"`file_exists`"},"2082":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-11","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"`max_tool_calls` (alias: `max_command_count`)"},"2083":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-12","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/setup#making-a-check-advisory-with-required","content":"Making a check advisory with `required`"},"2084":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-13","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/setup#how-a-cases-passfail-is-decided","content":"How a case's pass/fail is decided"},"2085":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-14","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/setup#4-validate-then-run-then-report","content":"4\\. Validate, then run, then report"},"2086":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-15","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/setup#setup-checklist","content":"Setup checklist"},"2087":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-16","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/evals-quality/setup#see-also","content":"See also"},"2088":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-17","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#eval-setup","content":"This page is the reference for **authoring** an eval suite: the config table in `skill-project.toml`, the prompts CSV a suite is made of, and the optional checks TOML that actually decides pass/fail. Work through it top to bottom once, then use Run evals for the day-to-day commands."},"2089":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-18","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#prerequisites","content":"`skill-project.toml` exists (project root or skill directory — `fastskill` walks up the tree to find it)."},"2090":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-19","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#prerequisites","content":"`SKILL.md` exists alongside it if you're authoring a single skill's suite."},"2091":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-20","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#prerequisites","content":"For `fastskill eval run`: a supported agent CLI on `PATH`. Agent keys come from aikit-sdk: `aikit`, `claude`, `codex`, `cursor`, `gemini`, and `pi`. A key is accepted only when its CLI is detected on the current machine; a typo and an uninstalled agent both error with `RUNTIME_UNKNOWN_ID`. `fastskill eval validate --all` reports which keys are detected in *your* environment."},"2092":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-21","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#prerequisites","content":"Evals do not require embedding or `OPENAI_API_KEY`; those are used by `index rebuild` and\n`skill search --local`."},"2093":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-22","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"Add this table to `skill-project.toml`. Every path is resolved relative to the **skill project root** (the directory containing `skill-project.toml`) unless it's absolute."},"2094":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-23","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"Field"},"2095":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-24","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"Type"},"2096":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-25","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"Required"},"2097":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-26","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"Default"},"2098":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-27","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"Meaning"},"2099":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-28","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"`prompts`"},"2100":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-29","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"path"},"2101":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-30","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"**yes**"},"2102":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-31","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"—"},"2103":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-32","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"Path to the prompts CSV."},"2104":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-33","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"`checks`"},"2105":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-34","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"path"},"2106":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-35","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"no"},"2107":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-36","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"none"},"2108":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-37","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"Path to the checks TOML. Omit it and there are no deterministic checks at all — see the callout below."},"2109":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-38","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"`timeout_seconds`"},"2110":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-39","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"integer"},"2111":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-40","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"no"},"2112":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-41","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"`900`"},"2113":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-42","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"Per-case timeout passed to the agent run."},"2114":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-43","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"`trials_per_case`"},"2115":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-44","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"integer"},"2116":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-45","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"no"},"2117":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-46","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"`1`"},"2118":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-47","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"Trials run per case; validated to `[1, 1000]` (`EVAL_INVALID_TRIALS_CONFIG` otherwise)."},"2119":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-48","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"`parallel`"},"2120":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-49","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"integer"},"2121":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-50","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"no"},"2122":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-51","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"unset (CPU core count)"},"2123":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-52","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"Max concurrent trials for one case."},"2124":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-53","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"`pass_threshold`"},"2125":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-54","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"float"},"2126":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-55","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"no"},"2127":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-56","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"`1.0`"},"2128":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-57","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"Fraction of trials that must pass for a case to be marked passed; validated to `[0.0, 1.0]` (`EVAL_INVALID_THRESHOLD` otherwise)."},"2129":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-58","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"`fail_on_missing_agent`"},"2130":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-59","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"bool"},"2131":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-60","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"no"},"2132":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-61","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"**`true`**"},"2133":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-62","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"If true, `eval run` and `eval validate --agent <key>` error with `EVAL_AGENT_UNAVAILABLE` when the chosen agent isn't installed."},"2134":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-63","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"**Defaults verified against source** (`crates/fastskill-core/src/core/manifest.rs::EvalConfigToml`): `timeout_seconds` defaults to **900**, and `fail_on_missing_agent` defaults to **true** — the CLI refuses to run against a missing agent unless you explicitly set it to `false`. Don't assume otherwise from older examples."},"2135":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-64","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#1-the-toolfastskilleval-table","content":"With no `checks` file configured, there is effectively no deterministic signal: a case passes purely on the agent process exiting `0`. Point `checks` at a real file once you want the suite to assert anything about *what* the agent did."},"2136":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-65","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#validate-the-config","content":"Real output against a working config (this one set `timeout_seconds = 120` and `fail_on_missing_agent = false`):"},"2137":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-66","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#validate-the-config","content":"(`parallel: 0` here just means \"unset\" in the table renderer — the runner still falls back to CPU core count.) A broken `checks.toml` fails validation immediately, e.g.:"},"2138":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-67","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#validate-the-config","content":"A prompts CSV missing a required column fails the same way:"},"2139":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-68","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"The suite loader (`aikit-evals::suite`) reads a header row with **required** columns `id`, `prompt`, `should_trigger`, plus optional `tags` and `workspace_subdir`."},"2140":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-69","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"Column"},"2141":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-70","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"Required"},"2142":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-71","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"Meaning"},"2143":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-72","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"`id`"},"2144":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-73","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"yes"},"2145":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-74","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"Non-empty identifier per row. Used for `--case`, artifact folder names, and reports."},"2146":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-75","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"`prompt`"},"2147":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-76","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"yes"},"2148":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-77","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"Text sent to the agent. Use CSV quoting (`\"...\"`, doubled `\"\"` for an embedded quote) for commas or newlines."},"2149":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-78","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"`should_trigger`"},"2150":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-79","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"yes"},"2151":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-80","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"`true`/`1` (case-insensitive `true`) or anything else counts as `false`. &#x2A;*See the callout below — this column does not affect pass/fail.**"},"2152":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-81","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"`tags`"},"2153":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-82","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"no"},"2154":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-83","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"Comma-separated tags inside the cell (e.g. `\"smoke,basic\"`). Used by `eval run --tag <name>`."},"2155":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-84","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"`workspace_subdir`"},"2156":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-85","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"no"},"2157":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-86","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"Relative path that becomes the agent's working directory for the case. Under the default isolation it is created **inside the case's scratch workspace**, with fixture files copied in from the same path under the project root; under `--no-isolation` it resolves directly under the project root. Empty or omitted → workspace root."},"2158":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-87","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"Empty lines are skipped."},"2159":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-88","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#2-the-prompts-csv","content":"**`should_trigger` is inert.** The field's own doc comment in `aikit-evals&#x60; says it plainly: &#x2A;\"Whether the skill should trigger (documentation-only; checks.toml is authoritative for pass/fail).\"* No scorer reads it. The same global check list from `checks.toml` runs against **every** case regardless of what `should_trigger` says, and with no checks file configured, pass/fail comes only from the agent process's exit code. There is currently no way to express a per-case \"this prompt must NOT trigger the skill\" expectation — treat the column as documentation for a human reader, not as a control the CLI acts on. Do not build a suite on the assumption that setting `should_trigger,false` makes the suite verify non-triggering; it does not."},"2160":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-89","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#3-checks-checkstoml-optional","content":"Point `checks` at a TOML file with one or more `[[check]]` tables, keyed by the required `name` field. There are exactly five check types (`aikit_evals::checks::CheckDefinition`):"},"2161":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-90","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#3-checks-checkstoml-optional","content":"**Checks score the canonical trace, never raw stdout.** Every check below matches against the run's `trace.jsonl` — the parsed, structured event stream. Raw stdout is deliberately excluded: with the `claude` agent it opens with a `system`/`project init` event listing **every skill installed in the environment**, which used to make any skill-name pattern pass vacuously. Assistant text still reaches the trace as message events, so matching on what the agent actually said continues to work."},"2162":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-91","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"The check you almost certainly want for \"did my skill fire?\"."},"2163":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-92","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"Field"},"2164":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-93","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"Type"},"2165":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-94","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"Required"},"2166":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-95","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"Default"},"2167":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-96","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"`skill`"},"2168":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-97","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"string"},"2169":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-98","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"no"},"2170":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-99","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"— (omit to match *any* skill invocation)"},"2171":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-100","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"`expected`"},"2172":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-101","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"bool"},"2173":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-102","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"no"},"2174":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-103","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"`true` (`false` asserts the skill did **not** run)"},"2175":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-104","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"`required`"},"2176":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-105","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"bool"},"2177":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-106","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"no"},"2178":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-107","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"`true`"},"2179":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-108","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#skill_invoked","content":"Matches a **structured `Skill` tool invocation** in the trace, not a substring of prose. When `skill` is given, it must **exactly equal** the invocation's skill-identifying input field (`skill`, `name`, or `skillName`) — `\"foo\"` does not match a `\"foo-bar\"` invocation, and a skill name merely mentioned in argument text does not count. This is the robust way to assert triggering — and, with `expected = false`, the only reliable way to assert non-triggering."},"2180":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-109","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"Field"},"2181":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-110","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"Type"},"2182":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-111","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"Required"},"2183":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-112","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"Default"},"2184":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-113","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"`pattern`"},"2185":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-114","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"string"},"2186":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-115","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"yes"},"2187":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-116","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"—"},"2188":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-117","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"`expected`"},"2189":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-118","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"bool"},"2190":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-119","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"yes"},"2191":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-120","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"— (`true` = pattern must appear, `false` = must NOT appear)"},"2192":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-121","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"`required`"},"2193":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-122","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"bool"},"2194":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-123","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"no"},"2195":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-124","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"`true`"},"2196":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-125","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#trigger_expectation","content":"Matches `pattern` as a **plain substring** against the JSONL trace. Prefer `skill_invoked` for asserting that a skill ran; treat `trigger_expectation` as the escape hatch for matching arbitrary text the agent produced."},"2197":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-126","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"Field"},"2198":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-127","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"Type"},"2199":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-128","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"Required"},"2200":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-129","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"Default"},"2201":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-130","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"`pattern`"},"2202":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-131","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"string"},"2203":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-132","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"yes"},"2204":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-133","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"—"},"2205":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-134","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"`required`"},"2206":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-135","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"bool"},"2207":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-136","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"no"},"2208":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-137","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"`true`"},"2209":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-138","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#command_contains","content":"Same trace substring search as `trigger_expectation`, without the pass/fail inversion — passes if the pattern is found anywhere in the trace."},"2210":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-139","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"Field"},"2211":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-140","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"Type"},"2212":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-141","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"Required"},"2213":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-142","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"Default"},"2214":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-143","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"`path`"},"2215":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-144","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"path"},"2216":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-145","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"yes"},"2217":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-146","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"—"},"2218":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-147","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"`required`"},"2219":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-148","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"bool"},"2220":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-149","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"no"},"2221":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-150","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"`true`"},"2222":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-151","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#file_exists","content":"Passes if `path` exists under the case's working directory — the case's scratch workspace under the default isolation (plus `workspace_subdir` when set), or the project root under `--no-isolation`."},"2223":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-152","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"Field"},"2224":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-153","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"Type"},"2225":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-154","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"Required"},"2226":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-155","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"Default"},"2227":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-156","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"`limit`"},"2228":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-157","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"integer"},"2229":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-158","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"yes"},"2230":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-159","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"—"},"2231":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-160","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"`required`"},"2232":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-161","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"bool"},"2233":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-162","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"no"},"2234":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-163","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"`true`"},"2235":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-164","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"Passes if the number of **tool invocations** the agent made is `<= limit`."},"2236":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-165","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"A tool invocation is a structured `tool_use` trace event, plus any `raw_json` trace line — the\nlatter covers backends that still emit tool calls as raw JSON instead of decoded tool events.\nAssistant text output, token-usage events, and unmodelled SDK event variants are **not** counted."},"2237":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-166","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#max_tool_calls-alias-max_command_count","content":"Results use `\"check_name\": \"max_tool_calls\"`. The per-case artifact field counting\nthese events is `command_count`."},"2238":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-167","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#making-a-check-advisory-with-required","content":"Every check type accepts `required` (default `true`). Setting `required = false` makes the check **advisory**: it still runs, and its result still appears in the run artifacts with its own `passed` value, but a failure does not fail the case."},"2239":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-168","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#making-a-check-advisory-with-required","content":"Use it for signal you want visible in reports without gating the suite on it."},"2240":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-169","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#how-a-cases-passfail-is-decided","content":"No `checks` file configured (or it loads zero checks): the case **passes** iff the agent process exits `0`."},"2241":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-170","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#how-a-cases-passfail-is-decided","content":"Any checks loaded: the case **passes** only if every **required** check's `passed` is `true`. Checks marked `required = false` are reported but never fail the case. Among required checks there is no partial credit and no threshold — they are all-or-nothing per case."},"2242":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-171","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#how-a-cases-passfail-is-decided","content":"A case whose checks are **all** advisory (`required = false`) has nothing that can fail it, so it passes as long as it does not time out. That is intentional, but it means an all-optional `checks.toml` is not a safety net."},"2243":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-172","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#how-a-cases-passfail-is-decided","content":"A trial that times out is always `error`, independent of checks."},"2244":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-173","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#how-a-cases-passfail-is-decided","content":"Across trials, `pass_threshold` decides the case's aggregated status: pass rate across trials must be `>= pass_threshold`."},"2245":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-174","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#4-validate-then-run-then-report","content":"Once the manifest, CSV, and checks file exist:"},"2246":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-175","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#4-validate-then-run-then-report","content":"`--output-dir` is **required** on `fastskill eval run` — there is no default. Omitting it fails argument parsing before anything else runs:"},"2247":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-176","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#4-validate-then-run-then-report","content":"`--agent <key>` (repeatable) and `--all` are mutually exclusive on both `eval run` and `eval validate` — passing both errors with `RUNTIME_CONFLICTING_FLAGS`. `eval run` additionally requires one of them (passing neither errors with `RUNTIME_NO_SELECTION`); on `eval validate` both are optional — omit them to validate config without checking any agent's availability."},"2248":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-177","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#4-validate-then-run-then-report","content":"See Run evals for the full day-to-day command set, artifact layout, and CI gating pattern."},"2249":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-178","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#setup-checklist","content":"`[tool.fastskill.eval]` present with a `prompts` path that resolves."},"2250":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-179","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#setup-checklist","content":"Prompts CSV has `id`, `prompt`, `should_trigger` headers (plus `tags` / `workspace_subdir` if you use them)."},"2251":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-180","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#setup-checklist","content":"You are **not** relying on `should_trigger` to gate pass/fail — it doesn't."},"2252":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-181","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#setup-checklist","content":"`checks.toml` exists if you want real scoring signal, and uses `skill_invoked` (not a bare-name `trigger_expectation`) to assert that your skill fired."},"2253":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-182","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#setup-checklist","content":"`fastskill eval validate --all` passes and lists the agent you intend to run against as available."},"2254":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-183","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#setup-checklist","content":"Output directory convention agreed for `--output-dir` (local + CI)."},"2255":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-184","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#see-also","content":"Run evals"},"2256":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-185","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#see-also","content":"Cluster analysis"},"2257":{"id":"/evals-quality/setup-186","page_id":"/evals-quality/setup","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/evals-quality/setup#see-also","content":"eval command"},"2258":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","type":"page","content":"Advanced Patterns","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Reference","Workflow examples"],"tags":[],"url":"/examples/advanced-patterns"},"2259":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-0","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns","content":"Analyze overlap, optimize skills, filter project groups, and manage editable and global skills."},"2260":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-1","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#overview","content":"Overview"},"2261":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-2","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#find-duplicate-and-overlapping-skills","content":"Find duplicate and overlapping skills"},"2262":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-3","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#improve-a-skill-with-optimization","content":"Improve a skill with `optimization`"},"2263":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-4","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#install-only-part-of-a-collection-with-groups","content":"Install only part of a collection with groups"},"2264":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-5","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#editable-and-recursive-local-skills","content":"Editable and recursive local skills"},"2265":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-6","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#project-vs-global-scope","content":"Project vs. global scope"},"2266":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-7","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#overview","content":"These are real, source-backed workflows for teams managing many skills. Every command below exists in\nthe CLI."},"2267":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-8","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#find-duplicate-and-overlapping-skills","content":"As a collection grows, skills drift into overlap. `fastskill analysis` surfaces that:"},"2268":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-9","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#find-duplicate-and-overlapping-skills","content":"`analysis duplicates` supports filtering and output control:"},"2269":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-10","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#find-duplicate-and-overlapping-skills","content":"Flag"},"2270":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-11","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#find-duplicate-and-overlapping-skills","content":"Purpose"},"2271":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-12","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#find-duplicate-and-overlapping-skills","content":"`--threshold`"},"2272":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-13","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#find-duplicate-and-overlapping-skills","content":"Minimum similarity to report"},"2273":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-14","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#find-duplicate-and-overlapping-skills","content":"`--limit`"},"2274":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-15","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#find-duplicate-and-overlapping-skills","content":"Maximum number of pairs to show"},"2275":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-16","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#find-duplicate-and-overlapping-skills","content":"`--severity`"},"2276":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-17","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#find-duplicate-and-overlapping-skills","content":"Filter by minimum severity: `critical`, `high`, `medium`, `all`"},"2277":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-18","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#find-duplicate-and-overlapping-skills","content":"`--format`"},"2278":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-19","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#find-duplicate-and-overlapping-skills","content":"`table`, `json`, `grid`, or `xml` (`--json` is shorthand)"},"2279":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-20","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#improve-a-skill-with-optimization","content":"`fastskill optimization` runs a text-gradient loop to iteratively improve a skill's content:"},"2280":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-21","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#install-only-part-of-a-collection-with-groups","content":"Skills can be tagged into groups; installs can include or exclude them (poetry-style):"},"2281":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-22","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#editable-and-recursive-local-skills","content":"For local skill development, add without copying and add whole trees at once:"},"2282":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-23","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#editable-and-recursive-local-skills","content":"After editing an editable skill in place, run `fastskill index rebuild` so semantic search and resolve\nreflect the changes."},"2283":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-24","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#project-vs-global-scope","content":"Most commands default to the current project. Use `--global` to operate on the shared user-level\nskills directory (`~/.config/fastskill/skills`, tracked by `global-skills.lock`):"},"2284":{"id":"/examples/advanced-patterns-25","page_id":"/examples/advanced-patterns","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/advanced-patterns#project-vs-global-scope","content":"Use `analysis` to keep a collection tidy, `optimization` to sharpen individual skills, and group\nfilters\nplus `--global` to control what gets installed where."},"2285":{"id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","page_id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","type":"page","content":"Integration Tutorials","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Reference","Workflow examples"],"tags":[],"url":"/examples/integration-tutorials"},"2286":{"id":"/examples/integration-tutorials-0","page_id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/integration-tutorials","content":"Connect FastSkill to agents and pipelines: MCP into Claude Code and Cursor, the serve HTTP API, and locked installs in CI."},"2287":{"id":"/examples/integration-tutorials-1","page_id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/examples/integration-tutorials#overview","content":"Overview"},"2288":{"id":"/examples/integration-tutorials-2","page_id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/examples/integration-tutorials#1-mcp-into-claude-code","content":"1\\. MCP into Claude Code"},"2289":{"id":"/examples/integration-tutorials-3","page_id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/examples/integration-tutorials#2-mcp-into-cursor","content":"2\\. MCP into Cursor"},"2290":{"id":"/examples/integration-tutorials-4","page_id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/examples/integration-tutorials#3-call-the-http-api-from-an-app","content":"3\\. Call the HTTP API from an app"},"2291":{"id":"/examples/integration-tutorials-5","page_id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/examples/integration-tutorials#4-reproducible-installs-in-ci","content":"4\\. Reproducible installs in CI"},"2292":{"id":"/examples/integration-tutorials-6","page_id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/integration-tutorials#overview","content":"These tutorials cover FastSkill's real integration surfaces: the **MCP** server for agents, the\n**HTTP API** from `fastskill server serve`, and **locked installs** in CI. Each uses commands and endpoints\nthat exist in the tool."},"2293":{"id":"/examples/integration-tutorials-7","page_id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/integration-tutorials#1-mcp-into-claude-code","content":"Expose FastSkill to Claude Code as MCP tools — read-only unless you start the server with\n`--enable-write`."},"2294":{"id":"/examples/integration-tutorials-8","page_id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/integration-tutorials#1-mcp-into-claude-code","content":"Claude Code will now see tools named after complete command paths, such as\n`fastskill_skill_search`, `fastskill_skill_list`, `fastskill_skill_read`, and\n`fastskill_repo_show`. Mutating tools such as `fastskill_project_install` and\n`fastskill_repo_add` are withheld until the server is started with `--enable-write`; see\nWrite access. To point the agent at a running HTTP MCP\nserver instead of spawning FastSkill itself:"},"2295":{"id":"/examples/integration-tutorials-9","page_id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/integration-tutorials#2-mcp-into-cursor","content":"Same flow, different agent key:"},"2296":{"id":"/examples/integration-tutorials-10","page_id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/integration-tutorials#2-mcp-into-cursor","content":"Supported agents: `claude`, `cursor`, `gemini`, `copilot`, `opencode`, `codex`. See the full\nMCP tool-calling guide."},"2297":{"id":"/examples/integration-tutorials-11","page_id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/integration-tutorials#3-call-the-http-api-from-an-app","content":"Run the server and use the versioned `/api/v1/...` REST surface. Start read-only:"},"2298":{"id":"/examples/integration-tutorials-12","page_id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/integration-tutorials#3-call-the-http-api-from-an-app","content":"These are all read endpoints and work without `--enable-write`. To manage skills over HTTP (install /\nupdate / delete), start with `fastskill server serve --enable-write`, and front the port with an\nauthenticating proxy if it is exposed — `server serve` enforces no auth of its own. See the\n`server serve` reference and security model."},"2299":{"id":"/examples/integration-tutorials-13","page_id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/integration-tutorials#4-reproducible-installs-in-ci","content":"Commit `skill-project.toml` and `skills.lock`, then install exact locked versions in the pipeline:"},"2300":{"id":"/examples/integration-tutorials-14","page_id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/integration-tutorials#4-reproducible-installs-in-ci","content":"Set `OPENAI_API_KEY` from a CI secret if the pipeline needs semantic search or reindex; without it\nthose steps skip silently rather than failing."},"2301":{"id":"/examples/integration-tutorials-15","page_id":"/examples/integration-tutorials","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/examples/integration-tutorials#4-reproducible-installs-in-ci","content":"For agents, install FastSkill as an MCP server. For services and pipelines, use the `server serve`\nHTTP API and `project install --lock`. There is no separate SDK to integrate — the CLI, MCP tools,\nand HTTP API are the surface."},"2302":{"id":"/integration/agents","page_id":"/integration/agents","type":"page","content":"Documentation and tools for agents","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Connect agents","Agent setup"],"tags":[],"url":"/integration/agents"},"2303":{"id":"/integration/agents-0","page_id":"/integration/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/agents","content":"Retrieve current FastSkill documentation as Markdown and use the CLI or MCP safely."},"2304":{"id":"/integration/agents-1","page_id":"/integration/agents","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/agents#read-the-documentation","content":"Read the documentation"},"2305":{"id":"/integration/agents-2","page_id":"/integration/agents","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/agents#inspect-the-cli-contract","content":"Inspect the CLI contract"},"2306":{"id":"/integration/agents-3","page_id":"/integration/agents","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/agents#preview-apply-verify","content":"Preview, apply, verify"},"2307":{"id":"/integration/agents-4","page_id":"/integration/agents","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/agents#agent-skills-and-mcp","content":"Agent skills and MCP"},"2308":{"id":"/integration/agents-5","page_id":"/integration/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/agents#read-the-documentation","content":"This site documents one release. The release number appears on every page and in\nall Markdown exports. Start with llms.txt, follow its per-page Markdown\nlinks, or download llms-full.txt. These URLs need no authentication\nor browser JavaScript. Each page also provides View Markdown and Copy Markdown."},"2309":{"id":"/integration/agents-6","page_id":"/integration/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/agents#inspect-the-cli-contract","content":"Match the binary version to the documentation. `cli spec` describes the installed\nbinary's complete command tree and flags. Use only the flags supported by that\ncommand; `--json` is not a global flag."},"2310":{"id":"/integration/agents-7","page_id":"/integration/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/agents#preview-apply-verify","content":"Check the process exit status and the returned diagnostics. A valid JSON response\ncan describe failure or partial success. Dry runs validate a plan without changing\nmanaged state; online plans can still fetch inputs. Use `--offline` when supported\nand when required verified content is already available locally."},"2311":{"id":"/integration/agents-8","page_id":"/integration/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/agents#agent-skills-and-mcp","content":"Installed skills provide task instructions. FastSkill's MCP tools provide package\noperations. They are separate interfaces; reading a skill does not require an MCP\nserver. See Claude Code and\nCursor for installation locations and registration."},"2312":{"id":"/integration/agents-9","page_id":"/integration/agents","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/agents#agent-skills-and-mcp","content":"The server exposes read-only tools by default. Mutating tools require\n`mcp serve --enable-write`. Tool names use the full command path, for example\n`fastskill_skill_read` and `fastskill_project_install`. See\nMCP tool access for write configuration."},"2313":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","type":"page","content":"Claude Code Integration","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Connect agents","Agent setup"],"tags":[],"url":"/integration/claude-code-integration"},"2314":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-0","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration","content":"Integrate FastSkill with Claude Code for intelligent skill discovery."},"2315":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-1","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#overview","content":"Overview"},"2316":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-2","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#quick-start","content":"Quick start"},"2317":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-3","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#how-it-works","content":"How it works"},"2318":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-4","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#github-actions","content":"GitHub Actions"},"2319":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-5","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"2320":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-6","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#mcp-registration","content":"MCP Registration"},"2321":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-7","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#http-api","content":"HTTP API"},"2322":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-8","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#overview","content":"Claude Code reads skills **directly** from the skills directory (`.claude/skills/` by\ndefault). FastSkill's job is to get the right skills onto disk and keep them reconciled with\nyour manifest — once a skill is installed, Claude Code discovers it natively. There is no\nmetadata file to generate or keep in sync."},"2323":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-9","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#quick-start","content":"That's it — the next time Claude Code runs in this project, the installed skills are available."},"2324":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-10","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#how-it-works","content":"`fastskill project install` / `fastskill skill add` materializes skills into the configured\n`skills_directory` (default `.claude/skills/`)."},"2325":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-11","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#how-it-works","content":"Each skill is a folder containing `SKILL.md` plus its resources."},"2326":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-12","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#how-it-works","content":"Claude Code scans that directory and loads skills by their `SKILL.md` frontmatter — no\nexport or sync step is involved."},"2327":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-13","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#how-it-works","content":"Use `fastskill skill read <skill-id>` to see exactly what an agent loads, or\n`fastskill skill read <skill-id> --meta` for just the metadata."},"2328":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-14","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#github-actions","content":"Keep the skills directory reconciled in CI so commits always carry the resolved skill set:"},"2329":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-15","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#troubleshooting","content":"**Claude Code doesn't see a skill:** Confirm it is installed with `fastskill skill list`, and that\nthe skills directory contains a valid `SKILL.md` for it. `fastskill skill read <skill-id>` should\nprint its content."},"2330":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-16","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#troubleshooting","content":"**Wrong skills directory:** Claude Code and FastSkill must agree on the location. The default\nis `.claude/skills/`; override it via `skills_directory` under `[tool.fastskill]` in\n`skill-project.toml` or the `--skills-dir` flag."},"2331":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-17","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#mcp-registration","content":"Register `fastskill` as an MCP server inside Claude Code with a single command:"},"2332":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-18","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#mcp-registration","content":"After running the command, reload Claude Code. The tools exposed by\n`fastskill mcp serve --transport stdio` will be callable from the agent — the read-only ones only.\nMutating tools (`fastskill_project_install`, `fastskill_skill_add`,\n`fastskill_skill_remove`, …) require `mcp serve --enable-write`; see\nWrite access."},"2333":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-19","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#http-api","content":"`fastskill server serve` exposes FastSkill's versioned application API under `/api/v1/…`, for example `GET /api/v1/status` and `GET /api/v1/skills`."},"2334":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-20","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#http-api","content":"The old Claude-compatible `/v1/skills…` HTTP surface is no longer part of the public server. Use the MCP integration above for Claude Code and use `/api/v1/…` for HTTP clients."},"2335":{"id":"/integration/claude-code-integration-21","page_id":"/integration/claude-code-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/claude-code-integration#http-api","content":"See the agent’s skill documentation for native discovery behavior."},"2336":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","type":"page","content":"Cursor Integration","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Connect agents","Agent setup"],"tags":[],"url":"/integration/cursor-integration"},"2337":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-0","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/cursor-integration","content":"Integrate FastSkill with Cursor IDE for intelligent skill discovery and tool recommendations."},"2338":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-1","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/cursor-integration#overview","content":"Overview"},"2339":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-2","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/cursor-integration#quick-start","content":"Quick start"},"2340":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-3","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/cursor-integration#mcp-registration","content":"MCP registration"},"2341":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-4","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/cursor-integration#how-cursor-uses-the-skills","content":"How Cursor uses the skills"},"2342":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-5","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/cursor-integration#example","content":"Example"},"2343":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-6","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/cursor-integration#configuration","content":"Configuration"},"2344":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-7","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/cursor-integration#multiple-skill-directories","content":"Multiple skill directories"},"2345":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-8","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/cursor-integration#automation","content":"Automation"},"2346":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-9","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/cursor-integration#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"2347":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-10","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/integration/cursor-integration#summary","content":"Summary"},"2348":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-11","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/cursor-integration#overview","content":"Cursor discovers skills **directly** from the skills directory (`.claude/skills/` by default)\nand via the FastSkill MCP server. FastSkill's job is to install the right skills onto disk and\nkeep them reconciled with your manifest — there is no metadata file to generate or keep in sync."},"2349":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-12","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/cursor-integration#overview","content":"Modern agents (Cursor, Claude Code, …) read installed skills from the skills directory natively.\nJust `fastskill project install` (or `fastskill skill add`) and the skills are available. Register the MCP\nserver below for richer, tool-based access from inside Cursor."},"2350":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-13","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/cursor-integration#mcp-registration","content":"Register `fastskill` as an MCP server inside Cursor with a single command:"},"2351":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-14","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/cursor-integration#mcp-registration","content":"After running the command, reload Cursor. The tools exposed by\n`fastskill mcp serve --transport stdio` will be callable from the agent — the read-only ones only.\nMutating tools (`fastskill_project_install`, `fastskill_skill_add`,\n`fastskill_skill_remove`, …) require\n`mcp serve --enable-write`; see Write access."},"2352":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-15","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/cursor-integration#how-cursor-uses-the-skills","content":"When you ask Cursor to perform a task, it:"},"2353":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-16","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/cursor-integration#how-cursor-uses-the-skills","content":"**Reads available skills** from the skills directory (and the FastSkill MCP server, if\nregistered)."},"2354":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-17","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/cursor-integration#how-cursor-uses-the-skills","content":"**Matches task requirements** against each skill's `description` frontmatter."},"2355":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-18","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/cursor-integration#how-cursor-uses-the-skills","content":"**Loads the full `SKILL.md`** for relevant skills to get instructions and parameters —\nthe same content `fastskill skill read <skill-id>` prints."},"2356":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-19","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/cursor-integration#example","content":"**User query:*&#x2A; &#x2A;\"Help me create a PowerPoint presentation for my quarterly review.\"*"},"2357":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-20","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/cursor-integration#example","content":"Cursor scans installed skills for presentation-related descriptions, finds a match (e.g.\n`pptx`), loads its `SKILL.md`, and follows the skill's instructions to complete the task."},"2358":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-21","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/cursor-integration#configuration","content":"Ensure your project has a `skill-project.toml` and that Cursor and FastSkill agree on the\nskills directory. The default is `.claude/skills/`; override it via `skills_directory` under\n`[tool.fastskill]` in `skill-project.toml` or the `--skills-dir` flag."},"2359":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-22","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/cursor-integration#automation","content":"Keep the skills directory reconciled in CI so commits always carry the resolved skill set:"},"2360":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-23","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/cursor-integration#troubleshooting","content":"**Cursor doesn't see a skill**"},"2361":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-24","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/cursor-integration#troubleshooting","content":"**Semantic search returns nothing**"},"2362":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-25","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/cursor-integration#troubleshooting","content":"**Check environment readiness**"},"2363":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-26","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/cursor-integration#summary","content":"FastSkill's Cursor integration provides:"},"2364":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-27","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/cursor-integration#summary","content":"**Direct skill discovery** — Cursor reads installed skills from the skills directory, no sync step"},"2365":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-28","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/cursor-integration#summary","content":"**MCP access** — register the FastSkill MCP server for tool-based access inside Cursor"},"2366":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-29","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/cursor-integration#summary","content":"**Reproducible installs** — `skill-project.toml` + `skills.lock` keep the skill set consistent across the team"},"2367":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-30","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/cursor-integration#summary","content":"**Optional semantic search** — `fastskill index rebuild` + `fastskill skill search --local` when an embedding provider is configured"},"2368":{"id":"/integration/cursor-integration-31","page_id":"/integration/cursor-integration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/integration/cursor-integration#summary","content":"See the agent’s skill documentation for native discovery behavior."},"2369":{"id":"/optimize/configuration","page_id":"/optimize/configuration","type":"page","content":"Configuration Reference","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Evaluate and optimize","Optimization"],"tags":[],"url":"/optimize/configuration"},"2370":{"id":"/optimize/configuration-0","page_id":"/optimize/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/optimize/configuration","content":"All fields in optimize.toml, with valid ranges, defaults, and guidance on choosing values."},"2371":{"id":"/optimize/configuration-1","page_id":"/optimize/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/optimize/configuration#configuration-reference","content":"Configuration Reference"},"2372":{"id":"/optimize/configuration-2","page_id":"/optimize/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/optimize/configuration#minimal-example","content":"Minimal example"},"2373":{"id":"/optimize/configuration-3","page_id":"/optimize/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/optimize/configuration#full-reference","content":"Full reference"},"2374":{"id":"/optimize/configuration-4","page_id":"/optimize/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/optimize/configuration#artifacts-and-data","content":"Artifacts and data"},"2375":{"id":"/optimize/configuration-5","page_id":"/optimize/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/optimize/configuration#agents","content":"Agents"},"2376":{"id":"/optimize/configuration-6","page_id":"/optimize/configuration","type":"heading","tags"