"url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#4-investigate-mismatches-promptly","content":"Version mismatches indicate manual changes or corruption. Investigate and resolve promptly to maintain consistency."},"3308":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-97","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#5-remove-extraneous-skills","content":"Remove or add extraneous skills to `skill-project.toml` to avoid confusion and ensure clean skill ecosystem."},"3309":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-98","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#troubleshooting","content":"**Skills directory incorrect**: Check that `skills_directory` under `[tool.fastskill]` in `skill-project.toml` points to correct location."},"3310":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-99","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#troubleshooting","content":"**skill-project.toml missing**: Create `skill-project.toml` or use `fastskill project init`."},"3311":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-100","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#troubleshooting","content":"**Resolution**: Run `fastskill project install` to install skills from manifest."},"3312":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-101","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#troubleshooting","content":"**Manual installations**: Skills may have been added outside FastSkill management."},"3313":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-102","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#troubleshooting","content":"**Resolution**: Add to `skill-project.toml` if intentional, or remove with `fastskill skill remove`."},"3314":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-103","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#troubleshooting","content":"**Prevention**: Always use `fastskill skill add` to install skills for proper tracking."},"3315":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-104","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#troubleshooting","content":"**Manual file changes**: Skills may have been updated manually (e.g., git pull)."},"3316":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-105","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#troubleshooting","content":"**Corrupted lockfile**: Lockfile may be out of sync with actual state."},"3317":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-106","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#troubleshooting","content":"**Resolution**: Run `fastskill project install --lock` to reinstall from lockfile, or `fastskill skill update` to update lockfile."},"3318":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-107","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#see-also","content":"Install Command - Install skills from manifest"},"3319":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-108","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#see-also","content":"Update Command - Update skills and lockfile"},"3320":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-109","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#see-also","content":"List Command - List skills with reconciliation status"},"3321":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-110","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#see-also","content":"Manifest System - Understanding skill-project.toml and skills.lock"},"3322":{"id":"/skill-management/reconciliation-111","page_id":"/skill-management/reconciliation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/reconciliation#see-also","content":"`project init` - Project initialization and setup"},"3323":{"id":"/skill-management/validation","page_id":"/skill-management/validation","type":"page","content":"Validate a skill","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Manage skills","Skills and projects"],"tags":[],"url":"/skill-management/validation"},"3324":{"id":"/skill-management/validation-0","page_id":"/skill-management/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/validation","content":"Check skill structure and installed state before an agent uses it."},"3325":{"id":"/skill-management/validation-1","page_id":"/skill-management/validation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/skill-management/validation#start-with-skillmd","content":"Start with SKILL.md"},"3326":{"id":"/skill-management/validation-2","page_id":"/skill-management/validation","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/skill-management/validation#validate-installation-and-state","content":"Validate installation and state"},"3327":{"id":"/skill-management/validation-3","page_id":"/skill-management/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/validation#start-with-skillmd","content":"A skill root contains `SKILL.md` with YAML frontmatter and instructions:"},"3328":{"id":"/skill-management/validation-4","page_id":"/skill-management/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/validation#start-with-skillmd","content":"The standard validator expects a lowercase name of 1–64 characters using letters,\ndigits, and single separating hyphens. The description must be nonempty and at most\n1024 characters. Name and description help an agent decide when to load the skill."},"3329":{"id":"/skill-management/validation-5","page_id":"/skill-management/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/validation#start-with-skillmd","content":"FastSkill derives identity from the skill metadata/name and uses a semantic version\nwhen resolving or packaging skills. Version metadata is optional for a minimal skill;\nFastSkill defaults an unspecified version to `1.0.0`. Set `metadata.version`\nexplicitly for a skill you distribute."},"3330":{"id":"/skill-management/validation-6","page_id":"/skill-management/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/validation#validate-installation-and-state","content":"After creating the source above, add it from a configured project:"},"3331":{"id":"/skill-management/validation-7","page_id":"/skill-management/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/validation#validate-installation-and-state","content":"Installation validates metadata and source contents. Reconciliation checks desired\nconstraints, locked facts, dependency ownership, and installed content. Editable\nlocal sources are reported as mutable rather than digest-verified."},"3332":{"id":"/skill-management/validation-8","page_id":"/skill-management/validation","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/skill-management/validation#validate-installation-and-state","content":"A successful structural check does not prove that instructions are safe or useful.\nReview scripts and resources, then use evals to measure\nbehavior on representative tasks. See reconciliation\nfor missing, changed, conflicting, and unverifiable installations."},"3333":{"id":"/testing/debugging","page_id":"/testing/debugging","type":"page","content":"Debugging Guide","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Reference","Diagnostics"],"tags":[],"url":"/testing/debugging"},"3334":{"id":"/testing/debugging-0","page_id":"/testing/debugging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/debugging","content":"Diagnose FastSkill setup and behavior with `fastskill cli doctor` and `--verbose` output."},"3335":{"id":"/testing/debugging-1","page_id":"/testing/debugging","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/testing/debugging#overview","content":"Overview"},"3336":{"id":"/testing/debugging-2","page_id":"/testing/debugging","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/testing/debugging#fastskill-cli-doctor","content":"`fastskill cli doctor`"},"3337":{"id":"/testing/debugging-3","page_id":"/testing/debugging","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/testing/debugging#verbose-output","content":"Verbose output"},"3338":{"id":"/testing/debugging-4","page_id":"/testing/debugging","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/testing/debugging#see-also","content":"See also"},"3339":{"id":"/testing/debugging-5","page_id":"/testing/debugging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/debugging#overview","content":"The two tools for debugging FastSkill are `fastskill cli doctor` — an environment/configuration health\ncheck — and the global `--verbose` / `-v` flag for detailed command output."},"3340":{"id":"/testing/debugging-6","page_id":"/testing/debugging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/debugging#fastskill-cli-doctor","content":"`cli doctor` inspects your environment and reports what is and isn't set up:"},"3341":{"id":"/testing/debugging-7","page_id":"/testing/debugging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/debugging#fastskill-cli-doctor","content":"It runs these checks:"},"3342":{"id":"/testing/debugging-8","page_id":"/testing/debugging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/debugging#fastskill-cli-doctor","content":"Check"},"3343":{"id":"/testing/debugging-9","page_id":"/testing/debugging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/debugging#fastskill-cli-doctor","content":"What it verifies"},"3344":{"id":"/testing/debugging-10","page_id":"/testing/debugging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/debugging#fastskill-cli-doctor","content":"`skills_dir`"},"3345":{"id":"/testing/debugging-11","page_id":"/testing/debugging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/debugging#fastskill-cli-doctor","content":"The skills directory exists and is a directory"},"3346":{"id":"/testing/debugging-12","page_id":"/testing/debugging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/debugging#fastskill-cli-doctor","content":"`project_toml`"},"3347":{"id":"/testing/debugging-13","page_id":"/testing/debugging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/debugging#fastskill-cli-doctor","content":"`skill-project.toml` is present (walk-up from cwd)"},"3348":{"id":"/testing/debugging-14","page_id":"/testing/debugging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/debugging#fastskill-cli-doctor","content":"`embedding_config`"},"3349":{"id":"/testing/debugging-15","page_id":"/testing/debugging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/debugging#fastskill-cli-doctor","content":"`[tool.fastskill.embedding]` is configured (semantic search / reindex enabled)"},"3350":{"id":"/testing/debugging-16","page_id":"/testing/debugging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/debugging#fastskill-cli-doctor","content":"`api_key`"},"3351":{"id":"/testing/debugging-17","page_id":"/testing/debugging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/debugging#fastskill-cli-doctor","content":"`OPENAI_API_KEY` is set (required for embeddings)"},"3352":{"id":"/testing/debugging-18","page_id":"/testing/debugging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/debugging#fastskill-cli-doctor","content":"`auth_token`"},"3353":{"id":"/testing/debugging-19","page_id":"/testing/debugging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/debugging#fastskill-cli-doctor","content":"An auth token is present (`FASTSKILL_AUTH_TOKEN` or `FASTSKILL_TOKEN`) for remote registry operations"},"3354":{"id":"/testing/debugging-20","page_id":"/testing/debugging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/debugging#fastskill-cli-doctor","content":"For machine-readable output (CI, scripts):"},"3355":{"id":"/testing/debugging-21","page_id":"/testing/debugging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/debugging#fastskill-cli-doctor","content":"Common findings and fixes:"},"3356":{"id":"/testing/debugging-22","page_id":"/testing/debugging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/debugging#fastskill-cli-doctor","content":"**`project_toml` failing** — run `fastskill project init` to create `skill-project.toml`."},"3357":{"id":"/testing/debugging-23","page_id":"/testing/debugging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/debugging#fastskill-cli-doctor","content":"**`embedding_config` / `api_key` failing** — add `[tool.fastskill.embedding]` and set\n`OPENAI_API_KEY`; without them semantic search and reindex are disabled (they skip silently, they\ndon't error)."},"3358":{"id":"/testing/debugging-24","page_id":"/testing/debugging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/debugging#fastskill-cli-doctor","content":"**`auth_token` failing** — set `FASTSKILL_AUTH_TOKEN` (or `FASTSKILL_TOKEN`) if you use a private\nregistry."},"3359":{"id":"/testing/debugging-25","page_id":"/testing/debugging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/debugging#verbose-output","content":"Add `--verbose` (or `-v`) to any command to see detailed diagnostic output about what FastSkill is\ndoing — useful for understanding install resolution, indexing, and registry access:"},"3360":{"id":"/testing/debugging-26","page_id":"/testing/debugging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/debugging#verbose-output","content":"Start with `fastskill cli doctor` to confirm the environment, then re-run the failing command with\n`--verbose` to see the detail."},"3361":{"id":"/testing/debugging-27","page_id":"/testing/debugging","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/debugging#see-also","content":"Troubleshooting — common issues and resolutions."},"3362":{"id":"/testing/framework","page_id":"/testing/framework","type":"page","content":"Testing Framework","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Reference","Diagnostics"],"tags":[],"url":"/testing/framework"},"3363":{"id":"/testing/framework-0","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework","content":"Test your skills with `fastskill eval` — validate configuration, run prompts against an agent, and score the results."},"3364":{"id":"/testing/framework-1","page_id":"/testing/framework","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/testing/framework#overview","content":"Overview"},"3365":{"id":"/testing/framework-2","page_id":"/testing/framework","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/testing/framework#configure-evals","content":"Configure evals"},"3366":{"id":"/testing/framework-3","page_id":"/testing/framework","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/testing/framework#the-eval-subcommands","content":"The eval subcommands"},"3367":{"id":"/testing/framework-4","page_id":"/testing/framework","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/testing/framework#see-also","content":"See also"},"3368":{"id":"/testing/framework-5","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#overview","content":"The way you test a skill in FastSkill is `fastskill eval`. You define eval cases in your project\nmanifest, run them against an agent, and score the results. There is no separate unit/mock harness —\neval is the testing framework."},"3369":{"id":"/testing/framework-6","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#configure-evals","content":"Evals are declared under `[tool.fastskill.eval]` in `skill-project.toml`:"},"3370":{"id":"/testing/framework-7","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#configure-evals","content":"`prompts` — path to a CSV of prompt cases to run."},"3371":{"id":"/testing/framework-8","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#configure-evals","content":"`checks` — path to a TOML file of checks applied to each result."},"3372":{"id":"/testing/framework-9","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#configure-evals","content":"`timeout_seconds` — per-case timeout."},"3373":{"id":"/testing/framework-10","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#configure-evals","content":"`fail_on_missing_agent` — when `true`, eval fails instead of skipping if the agent isn't found."},"3374":{"id":"/testing/framework-11","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#the-eval-subcommands","content":"Command"},"3375":{"id":"/testing/framework-12","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#the-eval-subcommands","content":"What it does"},"3376":{"id":"/testing/framework-13","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#the-eval-subcommands","content":"`fastskill eval validate`"},"3377":{"id":"/testing/framework-14","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#the-eval-subcommands","content":"Validates the eval configuration and referenced files before running"},"3378":{"id":"/testing/framework-15","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#the-eval-subcommands","content":"`fastskill eval run`"},"3379":{"id":"/testing/framework-16","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#the-eval-subcommands","content":"Runs the eval cases against an agent"},"3380":{"id":"/testing/framework-17","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#the-eval-subcommands","content":"`fastskill eval report`"},"3381":{"id":"/testing/framework-18","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#the-eval-subcommands","content":"Shows a report for a completed eval run"},"3382":{"id":"/testing/framework-19","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#the-eval-subcommands","content":"`fastskill eval score`"},"3383":{"id":"/testing/framework-20","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#the-eval-subcommands","content":"Scores results"},"3384":{"id":"/testing/framework-21","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#the-eval-subcommands","content":"Eval output supports `--format table|json` (no grid/xml for eval)."},"3385":{"id":"/testing/framework-22","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#the-eval-subcommands","content":"Start by pinning down what \"good\" looks like in your `checks.toml`, then iterate: `eval run` →\n`eval report` → adjust the skill → repeat."},"3386":{"id":"/testing/framework-23","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#see-also","content":"Evals & quality overview — the quality workflow and concepts."},"3387":{"id":"/testing/framework-24","page_id":"/testing/framework","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/testing/framework#see-also","content":"eval command reference — full flags and output details."},"3388":{"id":"/tool-calling/development","page_id":"/tool-calling/development","type":"page","content":"MCP Tool Calling","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Connect agents","MCP tools"],"tags":[],"url":"/tool-calling/development"},"3389":{"id":"/tool-calling/development-0","page_id":"/tool-calling/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tool-calling/development","content":"Expose FastSkill to agents as MCP tools with `fastskill mcp serve` (read-only by default, `--enable-write` to allow mutation), and wire them into Claude Code, Cursor, and other agents with `fastskill mcp install`."},"3390":{"id":"/tool-calling/development-1","page_id":"/tool-calling/development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/tool-calling/development#overview","content":"Overview"},"3391":{"id":"/tool-calling/development-2","page_id":"/tool-calling/development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/tool-calling/development#serve-fastskill-as-an-mcp-server","content":"Serve FastSkill as an MCP server"},"3392":{"id":"/tool-calling/development-3","page_id":"/tool-calling/development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/tool-calling/development#write-access","content":"Write access"},"3393":{"id":"/tool-calling/development-4","page_id":"/tool-calling/development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/tool-calling/development#transports","content":"Transports"},"3394":{"id":"/tool-calling/development-5","page_id":"/tool-calling/development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/tool-calling/development#install-into-an-agent","content":"Install into an agent"},"3395":{"id":"/tool-calling/development-6","page_id":"/tool-calling/development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/tool-calling/development#list-configured-mcp-servers","content":"List configured MCP servers"},"3396":{"id":"/tool-calling/development-7","page_id":"/tool-calling/development","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/tool-calling/development#see-also","content":"See also"},"3397":{"id":"/tool-calling/development-8","page_id":"/tool-calling/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tool-calling/development#overview","content":"FastSkill's tool/integration surface for agents is **MCP** (Model Context Protocol). You do not\nauthor custom tools inside FastSkill — instead, `fastskill mcp serve` exposes FastSkill CLI commands\nto an agent as MCP tools, and `fastskill mcp install` writes the server config into your agent's\nconfiguration."},"3398":{"id":"/tool-calling/development-9","page_id":"/tool-calling/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tool-calling/development#overview","content":"The server is **read-only by default**: the mutating commands are not exported as tools unless you\nstart it with `--enable-write`. See Write access below."},"3399":{"id":"/tool-calling/development-10","page_id":"/tool-calling/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tool-calling/development#serve-fastskill-as-an-mcp-server","content":"Each exported CLI command is registered as an MCP tool named `fastskill_<path>`, where the command\npath has its separators replaced by underscores. For example:"},"3400":{"id":"/tool-calling/development-11","page_id":"/tool-calling/development","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/tool-calling/development#serve-fastskill-as